{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for native naming delivery b779cf015857c90af601689fcb36980baf8c76f5, tree eb5f5d92f3bb168aa0148717fa750cab2701b00a. The naming-specific mechanisms are supported by the reviewed Source and retained checks. The delivery needs a coherent current-main integration before approval: its older CLI and generated Page inputs do not include the subsequently approved recovery and request-binding repairs. This is the integration duty already recorded in 611f515dbd385639745e5348847d40a89dda223d, not a reduction of naming functionality.\n\nP2: recut under the same implementation request 9cadddbccb4908a57e27693c5f80beab38487e4f and builder promise bf1de935d1e9ad214d7dc6ae039ff4a3459155d4 on current main, presently e0bf51f381bca0ccbc06ac191f4e5e0d71ecb971. Preserve the approved expired-selected-plan guidance and expired/late original replay assertions in commands.ts and install-cohort.test.ts. Extend the application-versus-Counting diagnostic and its test expectation to name shared-name explicitly. Preserve the later application, SDK, Counter, Page request-binding and plan 028 entries. The four paths changed on both lines are docs/cli.md, commands.ts, install-cohort.test.ts and the opaque generated Page asset; all 32 other current-main delta paths must remain intact. The asset must correspond to the composed Source, including the landed Page request-binding repair. Publish the complete new artifact set and obtain review of that exact head. Keep existing results and failed outcomes; perform only meaningful checks for the actual composition and the required candidate gate, without repeating unchanged sweeps.\n\nArchitecture: the reviewed contribution creates an explicit register7/directory7/membership6/rules3/destination3/inbox1 cohort while retaining old pins and NEWEST. Directory7 retains the complete application factory. One revisioned native room-profile separates mutable display text from repository identity. Native membership delegation